{"type":"plan","title":"Two Cups at Dawn","logline":"A grandmother's forty-year ritual of pouring two teas becomes a bridge for her granddaughter to meet the grandfather she never knew.","shots":[{"index":1,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Early morning, cold rain mist over the lake. The tea house sits on stilts, lanterns glowing behind paper screens. Through the screens Grandma Hoa is visible at the low table, pouring tea into two cups. Steam rises.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Forty years, two cups, every dawn."},{"index":2,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Interior, warm lantern light. Grandma places the second cup on the window seat cushion, pauses, and touches the chipped rim with her thumb. The jade bangle catches the glow.","mode":"still","dialogue":"One for him, one for me."},{"index":3,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Lan enters shaking rain from a clear umbrella, framed over Grandma's shoulder. Water drips from the umbrella rim. Lan's red star clip is askew. She looks at the two cups, curious.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Bà, why two cups?"},{"index":4,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Golden dusk memory hue. Same tea house, brighter. Young Grandma sits at the window seat reading the indigo poem book. Young Husband approaches with two cups, trips on the threshold, tea arcs and splashes across the open pages.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Clumsy hands, beautiful words."},{"index":5,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Tea stain blooming on the poem page like ink blossom. Young Grandma's hand covers his ink-stained thumb. Both faces tilt up, laughing silently. Lantern light paints them gold.","mode":"still","dialogue":"Now it's ours."},{"index":6,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Present interior, rainy grey light. Lan climbs onto the window seat, picks up the chipped cup, sips. Grandma watches from the table, hands folded, eyes wide with surprise.","mode":"still","dialogue":"Tastes like rain and jasmine."},{"index":7,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Grandma's face: crinkles deepen at the eyes, mouth opens in a silent laugh — the first in years. Warmth floods the lantern light on her cheeks. The jade bangle glints.","mode":"still","dialogue":null},{"index":8,"shotType":"Slow zoom-in","description":"Golden dusk returns. Exterior wide shot of tea house on the lake, lanterns lit, water rippling gently. Through the window the two cups sit side by side on the low table, steam merging.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Some rituals bring ghosts home."}]}
